## Exp51 — Within-Day Exit-Risk Geometry Transport — UNDERPOWERED_WITHIN_DAY_CELL

Exact frozen Exp50/Exp49 replay PASS; Exp49 JOINT4 identifiability PASS; Exp27 untouched. Same original TRAIN-fitted JOINT4_EXIT; no refit/recalibration/new feature.

Formal target: same-BRT-day EXIT-vs-NO_EXIT concordance only, 8 environments x H={15,30,60,120}=32 cells. Whole-day bootstrap; cell requires both classes overall, >=2 contributing days, >=2 mixed-class days, >=9500/10000 valid replicates, and CI95 lower bound of WITHIN_DAY_AUC >0.5.

Formal cells passing: 15/32. Status:
EXP51_WITHIN_DAY_CELL_STATUS=UNDERPOWERED_WITHIN_DAY_CELL
EXP51_FORMAL_CELLS_PASS=15/32
WITHIN_DAY_GEOMETRY_RANKING_TRANSPORT=UNDERPOWERED_WITHIN_DAY_CELL
ROBUST_WITHIN_DAY_EXIT_URGENCY_ORDERING=UNDERPOWERED_WITHIN_DAY_CELL
EXP51_FORMAL_STATUS=UNDERPOWERED_WITHIN_DAY_CELL

Important diagnostics: pooled JOINT4 AUC remained strong, but within-day discrimination degraded materially in several environments/horizons. VALIDATION_EARLY__FULL_DOWN had WITHIN_AUC H60=.392786 and H120=.337430; VALIDATION_LATE__FULL_DOWN H15=.580531 with CI crossing .5 and H120 had only one mixed-class day; TEST_LATE__FULL_UP H30/H60/H120 also failed. Day-regime correlation between daily mean JOINT4 score and daily EXIT rate was often large, roughly +.60 to +.92 in many cells.

Interpretation: symmetric corridor geometry is not established as a universal timing or urgency law, even after conditioning comparisons to the same BRT day. The geometry family is CLOSED for further rescue in the historical universe. Do not subset horizons/environments or refit by side/time. Exp49/50/51 diagnostics remain descriptive only.

## Exp52 — Causal Intraday Regime Timing Family — FROZEN BEFORE SCORE

Purpose: test a genuinely new timing family motivated by Exp50/51 evidence that between-day/intraday regime composition carries substantial EXIT timing information. This is not a JOINT4 rescue and uses no corridor-geometry timing predictor.

Exact universe remains unchanged: replay exact Exp49 backbone; same historical cutoff; same Exp41 eligible 15/30/60/120m cells; same eight Exp44/45 direction x time environments; same binary EXIT-vs-NO_EXIT target; whole-BRT-day inference; TRAIN-only model fit; Exp27 untouched.

All Exp52 state features are computed causally from M5 information available at or before state_time within the same BRT day:
R1 TOD_SIN = sin(2*pi*minute_of_day/1440).
R2 TOD_COS = cos(2*pi*minute_of_day/1440).
R3 LOG_DAY_RANGE_ATR = log1p((cum_high_day - cum_low_day)/ATR_state).
R4 LOG_DAY_PATH_ATR = log1p(cumulative intraday absolute price path / ATR_state), where first bar contribution is abs(close-open) and later contributions are abs(close_t-close_{t-1}) within the same BRT day.
R5 DAY_EFFICIENCY = abs(close_state - first_open_day) / cumulative intraday absolute price path, with 0 when path=0; bounded numerically to [0,1].

Frozen candidate blocks:
TOD_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + TOD_SIN + TOD_COS.
RANGE_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + LOG_DAY_RANGE_ATR.
PATH_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + LOG_DAY_PATH_ATR.
EFF_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + DAY_EFFICIENCY.
JOINT5_EXIT = BASE_EXIT + all five frozen columns.
Drop-one diagnostics remove exactly one frozen candidate block from JOINT5: DROP_TOD, DROP_RANGE, DROP_PATH, DROP_EFF.

All models are binary discrete-time EXIT hazards with the same 24 elapsed-future-step intercepts used by Exp49, fit on TRAIN only. BASE_EXIT is the exact original Exp49 baseline. No standardization is used. JOINT5 numerical identifiability requires TRAIN design full column rank, converged fit, and finite coefficients.

Required analysis: TRAIN-only feature correlation/rank/condition; marginal candidate diagnostics with Holm correction across 4 candidate blocks x 8 environments x 2 metrics = 64 tests; JOINT5; drop-one; horizon 15/30/60/120 point gains; EXIT AUC and calibration; whole-BRT-day bootstrap. Marginal/drop-one/AUC/calibration are diagnostic only.

Primary formal comparison: JOINT5_EXIT vs exact BASE_EXIT on EXIT_STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED cells, pooled over the four frozen horizons within each exact environment. Metrics: binary Brier and LogLoss. Environment must contain EXIT and NO_EXIT and >=2 BRT days.

Formal gate: INTRADAY_REGIME_TIMING_FAMILY=PASS only if all 8 environments are scorable, JOINT5 is numerically identifiable, and JOINT5 beats BASE with CI95 lower bound >0 for Brier and LogLoss in all 8 environments = 16/16. ROBUST_INTRADAY_EXIT_CLOCK_CONTEXT and EXP52_FORMAL_STATUS use the same 16/16 gate.

Anti-rescue: no corridor geometry timing feature; no Dwell; no signed Position timing predictor; no alternate day boundary; no future/day-complete statistics; no alternate transforms after result; no added feature; no horizon subset; no dropped environment; no side/era-specific fit; no interaction/recalibration/intercept/threshold rescue; no Validation/TEST refit; no Exp27 scoring/modification.

Exp52 failure cannot erase Exp44/45/47 PASS results. Historical OOS remains exploratory; fresh-forward Exp27 remains decisive before runtime promotion.